AnnotMovie::draw() built the poster appearance, which stays cached in the
annotation, on gfx->getXRef(). page_renderer::render_page() draws through
Page::displaySlice() with copyXRef, so that XRef is a temporary copy freed
when the page is done; FontInfoScanner (page::text_list, document::fonts)
later fetched the poster through the freed XRef (heap-use-after-free in
XRef::fetch). Build the appearance on the document's XRef, as createForm()
and the other annotation types do.

